WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.280
When does Banker’s algorithm grant

2
00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:04.660
a request? Availability is only

3
00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:06.760
one gate: the request must

4
00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:08.540
also respect the process remaining

5
00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:09.960
claim and leave a safe

6
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:11.940
state. The safety check uses

7
00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.660
a provisional snapshot that must

8
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.200
be restored if the request

9
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:15.980
is refused.

10
00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:18.860
First compare Request with Need

11
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:21.560
component by component. A request

12
00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:23.680
beyond the declared remaining maximum

13
00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.220
is an invalid claim under

14
00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:27.020
this model. Do not merely

15
00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:28.780
wait for extra resources and

16
00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:30.540
silently increase the maximum.

17
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.980
Next compare Request with Available.

18
00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:36.440
If a requested component exceeds

19
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.300
the free amount, the process

20
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.960
must wait without making a

21
00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:42.560
provisional grant. Passing this gate

22
00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:45.760
establishes immediate availability, not safety.

23
00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:48.620
For the lecture snapshot, P

24
00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:51.040
one requests one, zero, two.

25
00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:52.940
Its original Need is one,

26
00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.520
two, two, and Available is

27
00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:57.180
three, three, two. The request

28
00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:59.100
fits both, so proceed to

29
00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.080
the provisional state.

30
00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.700
Subtract the request from Available

31
00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.140
to obtain two, three, zero.

32
00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:06.740
Add it to P one

33
00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:07.740
Allocation to obtain three, zero,

34
00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:10.080
two, and subtract it from

35
00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:11.900
Need to obtain zero, two,

36
00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.520
zero. All three changes describe

37
00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:16.040
the same provisional transfer.

38
00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:18.120
Run the safety test from

39
00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:20.180
that new state. P one

40
00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:21.760
can finish first, and a

41
00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:23.900
full completion sequence still exists,

42
00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:25.320
so the request can commit.

43
00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:27.700
A safety simulation is evidence

44
00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:30.100
of possible future completion, not

45
00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:31.420
a command to execute those

46
00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:33.280
processes immediately in that order.

47
00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.460
Now start from the committed

48
00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:37.700
state, not the original slide

49
00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:40.040
snapshot. As an added illustration,

50
00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:42.220
let P zero request zero,

51
00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:44.860
two, zero. This request fits

52
00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:46.620
both its remaining Need and

53
00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:48.800
the currently free vector, yet

54
00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.960
its provisional allocation leaves Available

55
00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:53.140
two, one, zero.

56
00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:55.440
No unfinished process can meet

57
00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:57.020
its remaining Need from two,

58
00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:58.880
one, zero in that provisional

59
00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:00.440
state. The request is available

60
00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:02.000
but unsafe, so it must

61
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.520
wait. Restore Available, Allocation and

62
00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:06.440
Need together; a partial rollback

63
00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:07.820
corrupts the resource snapshot.

64
00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.180
Keep three outcomes distinct: an

65
00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:13.980
invalid claim, an unavailable request,

66
00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:16.580
and an available but unsafe

67
00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:19.380
request. Only the last requires

68
00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:21.480
a trial allocation followed by

69
00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.680
a failed safety test. An

70
00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:25.580
unsafe decision is about preserving

71
00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:28.060
a completion guarantee, not proving

72
00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:29.060
a present deadlock.

73
00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:30.880
Things to take note of.

74
00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:33.000
Check the claim, check availability,

75
00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:36.220
update all three structures provisionally,

76
00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:38.280
then commit only if safe.

77
00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:40.360
Later requests begin from the

78
00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.260
latest committed state, and a

79
00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:44.180
refused trial leaves that state

80
00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:44.900
unchanged.
